The Golden Boost pedal's sound: Jatin Chowdhury's KlonCentaur circuit model
(https://github.com/jatinchowdhury18/KlonCentaur, commit
f3bb633a593b6fbb22a44c1ef9d1dbedbfe92d5b), BSD 3-clause (LICENSE).

Kept, unchanged: ChowCentaur/CommonProcessors and the circuit model in
ChowCentaur/GainStageProcessors (without GainStageProc.*, which needs the
plugin's parameter tree; src/engine/KlonCentaurDsp.cpp does what it and
ChowCentaurPlugin.cpp do, in the same order). Not used: the plugin itself,
its GUI, the neural-network gain stage (RTNeural) and toms917.

chowdsp_utils/ holds the four parts of chowdsp_utils
(https://github.com/Chowdhury-DSP/chowdsp_utils, commit
4830738ff7e2b7e0def7036fa3b0d8f75e2983f8, the one KlonCentaur uses) the
model needs, unchanged: the WDF headers (DSP/WDF/wdf.h, wdf_t.h, omega.h,
signum.h) and two filter headers (DSP/Filters/chowdsp_IIRFilter.h,
chowdsp_BilinearUtils.h). chowdsp_utils was GPL 3 at that commit
(chowdsp_utils/LICENSE).

ikaros/pch.h is ours: it stands in for ChowCentaur's precompiled header,
which every file of the model includes. The model's diode clipper also
calls wrightomega() from toms917 (whose license isn't clear) to fill a
lookup table; KlonCentaurDsp.cpp has its own for the real numbers needed.
